{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And Cain went out from before HaShem.</b> A parallel: 'And Mordecai went out from before the king' — He extended his life on account of his exile, and he too accepted His decree upon himself." "<b>And he settled in the land of Nod.</b> At first it is written 'you shall be נע ונד in the land,' but in the end it is written <b>in the land of Nod</b>, and it does not write נע. From this, exile atones for half."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:56.026857477Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}